{{! See docs/templates-reference.md. Drops the stock delegate pattern entirely: the generated
    class extends CrudController directly, inheriting every REST mapping from the Allcrud base
    class, so this file only needs to implement the getService()/getConverter() hooks.

    allcrudEntityName / allcrudPojoClassName / allcrudIdType / allcrudBasePath are resolved by
    AllcrudSpringCodegen#postProcessOperationsWithModels (a custom CodegenConfig, not the
    stock "spring" one) by inspecting the actual OpenAPI model - not hardcoded here anymore.

    See docs/adr/0005-basepath-absolute-not-concatenated.md and
    docs/adr/0001-generate-once-never-overwrite.md for @RequestMapping being a plain string
    literal (allcrudBasePath) instead of the stock Spring property placeholder.
    See docs/adr/0006-entity-out-of-scope-v1.md for allcrudEntityName/allcrudEntityPackage
    resolution.
    Service and Converter are NOT necessarily in this same package anymore - each of the 5
    layers has its own independent target package in allcrud-generator.yml's "packages"
    section, so they're imported explicitly via allcrudServicePackage/allcrudConverterPackage,
    same as the entity/POJO. This used to assume "same package, no import needed", which broke
    the instant a real yml put controller/service in different packages - never caught before
    because every test happened to use the same package for all 4 non-POJO layers.
    Generated class name is prefixed with allcrudEntityName ("Product"), not the stock
    per-tag classname variable ("ProductsApi" - derived from the OpenAPI tag, plural, with
    an "Api" suffix SpringCodegen adds by convention) - that mismatch was a naming bug
    fixed after the fact, not an intentional customization.

    @RestController, unconditionally - NOT the stock useResponseEntity-driven
    @Controller/@RestController branch (removed here). That branch's stock premise is that
    EVERY generated method's return type follows the same useResponseEntity choice (either
    every endpoint wraps in ResponseEntity, or none do) - true in the stock delegate pattern,
    where this file itself generates every method signature. It's false here: this class
    extends CrudController and inherits its FIXED method set from the core, unconditionally
    (not generated per spec), and that set already mixes bare-VO returns (create/update/
    findById/etc) with a ResponseEntity-wrapped one (findAll) in the same class. A bare
    @Controller (no @ResponseBody) only serializes ResponseEntity-returning methods correctly -
    every bare-VO method falls back to Spring MVC's view-resolution path instead of writing
    JSON, silently returning an empty body with HTTP 201/200/etc (looks like success in a
    quick check, breaks on read). Confirmed via a real booted Spring context + MockMvc, not
    assumed - useResponseEntity's stock default made every controller in this project's history
    "@Controller" and none of the bare-VO endpoints ever wrote a real response body until now,
    invisible because nothing before *ControllerIT ever exercised the actual HTTP layer. }}
package {{package}};

